                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0185ab1e-4b10-3d85-9f0e-2123d54fd36a",
                        "entry_id": "3c324c2a-580f-31ff-b3e2-9ad7550b1cb7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "to get even"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "463d70a6-fec8-4766-a559-11442b668133",
                                "sense_id": "0185ab1e-4b10-3d85-9f0e-2123d54fd36a",
                                "text": "— А, посто́й, голу́бчик, я поквита́юсь с тобо́й — вме́сто Мари́ны! — зло́бно говори́л он, — смотри́, пожа́луй, в кали́тку ле́зет: а я там, как пень, карау́лю у плетня́!..",
                                "translation": "“Just stay right there, young fellow, I’m going to get even with you – you were expecting Marina, and you got me instead!” he said threateningly. “She’s probably sneaking in through the wicket gate, and there I am, like a dummy, keeping watch by the wattle fence.”",
                                "english": "“Just stay right there, young fellow, I’m going to get even with you – you were expecting Marina, and you got me instead!” he said threateningly. “She’s probably sneaking in through the wicket gate, and there I am, like a dummy, keeping watch by the wattle fence.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
